  "findings": [
    "An ordered stream still pauses when delivery is held after local TLS has accepted the data. With an 80 ms relay stall, maximum delivery gaps range from 81.025 to 88.133 ms.",
    "Both action edges and their positions survive the delay. Old positions required by an intervening click or key must not be discarded. Motion-only cases are reported separately.",
    "Receive-side coalescing reduces redundant motion after delivery resumes, but cannot eliminate the interval while no new input reaches the destination."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One-second synthetic cases on a single Mac, with both roles in memory; not native Windows execution",
    "Delay is assigned to ciphertext reads and kept in FIFO order, not to individual IP packets. The relay does not model TCP congestion or retransmission.",
    "The 80 ms hold is deliberately injected; this does not attribute the real household mouse microcuts to the router.",
    "Each run has ordinary process scheduling variation. These measurements are not a guarantee of physical latency or smoothness."
  ],
  "next_steps": [
    "Measure actual per-stage input delivery in the jointly installed final candidate.",
    "Compare an authenticated loss-tolerant motion path only in a separate experiment, preserving ordered actions, focus, click positions, replay rejection and fallback. No transport or firewall change has been made here."
  ]
}
